.\" Man page for the check_cert Django management command
.\" scd-check-cert(1)
.TH SCD\-CHECK\-CERT 1 "2026-10-20" "SCD Effort Reporting" "SCD Effort Reporting Commands"
.SH NAME
scd\-check\-cert \- monitor TLS certificates for revocation, expiry and trust failures, and mail an alert
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python manage.py check_cert
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]]...
[\fB\-\-to\fR \fIEMAIL\fR]...
[\fB\-\-warn\-days\fR \fIDAYS\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-alert\-on\-unknown\fR | \fB\-\-ignore\-unknown\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-email\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-send\-test\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B check_cert
connects to each host the way a browser does, takes the certificate it is
served, and runs five checks:
.TP 12
.B connect
A TLS handshake completes.
.TP
.B trust
The chain, hostname included, verifies against the system CA bundle.
.TP
.B name
The subjectAltName covers the host. A wildcard covers exactly one leftmost
label. A failure here together with an OKD wildcard issuer means the router is
serving its default certificate rather than the Route's.
.TP
.B expiry
The certificate is valid now and has at least
.I DAYS
days left.
.TP
.B revocation
The issuing CA is downloaded from the certificate's AIA CA Issuers URL and
confirmed to have signed the leaf. OCSP is asked first. If OCSP gives no
usable answer, the CRL is fetched and searched for the serial.
.PP
Each check ends
.BR OK ,
.B PROBLEM
or
.BR UNKNOWN .
.B UNKNOWN
means the answer could not be established, for example both OCSP and the CRL
unreachable.
.PP
The command runs unattended, so it trusts revocation data only after checking
its signature:
.IP \(bu 2
An OCSP response must be signed by the issuing CA, or by a responder certificate
the CA issued with the OCSPSigning extended key usage (RFC 6960 \(sc4.2.2.2).
.IP \(bu 2
A CRL must be signed by the issuing CA.
.IP \(bu 2
Stale responses and CRLs (past their next-update time) are ignored.
.PP
A forged or stale "good" therefore cannot hide a revocation.
.PP
If any host is
.BR PROBLEM ,
or
.B UNKNOWN
while unknowns alert, one mail goes to the recipients with the full report and
the remediation commands. The subject line names the host and the first failing
check, for example:
.PP
.RS
.EX
[SCD Reporting] TLS certificate PROBLEM: scd\-reporting.fnal.gov \(em
revocation: REVOKED at 2026\-10\-19 14:34:14 UTC, reason superseded (OCSP ...)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Mail goes through the application's normal SMTP settings
.RB ( EMAIL_HOST ", " EMAIL_PORT ", ...)"
from
.BR DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL .
The command does not touch the database.
.PP
This is the unattended counterpart of
.BR check\-cert (1),
which an operator runs with
.B oc
access to look at, and reissue, the cert-manager side.
.SH OPTIONS
Each option overrides the corresponding environment variable, which in turn
overrides
.IR config/cert_monitor.yaml :
.PP
.RS
command line > environment > .env > config/cert_monitor.yaml > default
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST" \fR[:\fIPORT\fR]
Host to check; repeat for several. Port defaults to 443.
Overrides
.BR CERT_MONITOR_HOSTS ,
which defaults to
.BR SCD_HOSTNAME .
.TP
.BI \-\-to " EMAIL"
Alert recipient; repeat for several. Overrides
.BR CERT_MONITOR_RECIPIENTS .
.TP
.BI \-\-warn\-days " DAYS"
Alert when fewer days than this are left. Overrides
.BR CERT_MONITOR_WARN_DAYS .
Default 21.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Network timeout per request. Overrides
.BR CERT_MONITOR_TIMEOUT .
Default 15.
.TP
.BR \-\-alert\-on\-unknown ", " \-\-ignore\-unknown
Whether an
.B UNKNOWN
revocation status raises an alert. Overrides
.BR CERT_MONITOR_ALERT_ON_UNKNOWN .
Default: alert.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-email
Report on standard output only.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the mail that would be sent instead of sending it.
.TP
.B \-\-send\-test
Send the report mail even when every check passes, to prove that delivery
works end to end.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing to alert on.
.TP
.B 1
An alert was raised, and mailed unless
.B \-\-no\-email
or
.B \-\-dry\-run
was given.
.TP
.B 2
An alert was needed but could not be delivered (no recipients, or SMTP
failed), or there were no hosts to check.
.PP
In the CronJob, a non-zero exit marks the Job
.BR Failed ,
so a problem is visible in
.B oc get jobs
even if the mail is lost.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CERT_MONITOR_HOSTS
Comma-separated host[:port] list.
.TP
.B CERT_MONITOR_RECIPIENTS
Comma-separated addresses.
.TP
.B CERT_MONITOR_WARN_DAYS
.TQ
.B CERT_MONITOR_TIMEOUT
.TQ
.B CERT_MONITOR_ALERT_ON_UNKNOWN
See OPTIONS.
.TP
.B SCD_CONFIG_DIR
Directory holding
.IR cert_monitor.yaml .
Default
.IR config/ .
.SH DEPLOYMENT
On OKD the Helm chart runs the command from the
.B <release>\-cert\-monitor
CronJob. In
.IR my\-values.yaml :
.PP
.RS
.EX
certMonitor:
  enabled: true
  recipients: "someone@fnal.gov,other@fnal.gov"
  # hosts: ""                  # default: route.hostname
  # schedule: "15 */6 * * *"   # America/Chicago
.EE
.RE
.PP
The chart refuses to render when the monitor is enabled with no recipients.
While a problem persists the alert repeats on every run, so the schedule also
sets how often it repeats.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the site and print the report, sending nothing:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python manage.py check_cert \-\-no\-email
.EE
.RE
.PP
Prove that alert mail reaches you, from inside the cluster. The web pod runs the
same image with the same SMTP settings; the recipients are only in the CronJob,
so name one.
.RB ( "oc create job \-\-from=cronjob/..."
cannot override the command.)
.PP
.RS
.EX
oc exec \-n scd\-reporting deploy/web \-\- \e
  python manage.py check_cert \-\-send\-test \-\-to you@fnal.gov
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run the CronJob once now, exactly as scheduled (mails only on a problem):
.PP
.RS
.EX
oc create job cert\-monitor\-now \-n scd\-reporting \e
  \-\-from=cronjob/scd\-reporting\-cert\-monitor
oc logs \-n scd\-reporting \-f job/cert\-monitor\-now
oc delete job \-n scd\-reporting cert\-monitor\-now
.EE
.RE
.PP
See the mail a revoked certificate would produce, against a public test host:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python manage.py check_cert \-\-host revoked.badssl.com \e
  \-\-to you@fnal.gov \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
